# FastAPI Backend Skill

## Stack

* FastAPI
* Python 3.11
* Pydantic
* SQLAlchemy
* PostgreSQL

## Architecture

Use layered architecture:

* routers
* services
* repositories
* schemas
* models

## Folder Structure

```
backend/
 ├── app/
 │    ├── routers/
 │    ├── services/
 │    ├── repositories/
 │    ├── models/
 │    ├── schemas/
 │    └── core/
```

## API Rules

* Use async endpoints
* Use dependency injection
* Validate all request bodies
* Return proper HTTP status codes
* Never put business logic inside routers

## Coding Style

* Use type hints everywhere
* Use snake_case
* Use small functions
* Add docstrings for complex logic

## Database Rules

* Use SQLAlchemy ORM
* Avoid raw SQL unless necessary
* Use repository pattern

## Response Format

Standard API response:

```
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {},
  "message": "Success"
}
```

## Error Handling

* Use HTTPException
* Never expose internal stack traces
* Return meaningful error messages
